      "sourceTextSha256": "e353bad4dafdbb1526b9c75d59bd27984e34550520adfa1aedb564009a87e07e",
      "text": "Day 3 · Breakfast, then a private full-day tour (12 hours) with an English-speaking guide through the Cundiboyacense highlands and their imposing mountains. Visit the Salt Cathedral of Zipaquirá, built inside a mine 180 metres deep and considered one of Colombia’s great wonders of engineering and religious art; the Basilica of Chiquinquirá; and Ráquira, known for its architecture and crafts. Continue to Villa de Leyva, a colonial town surrounded by mountains and desert, with one of the largest squares in Colombia. Typical lunch included. Overnight in Villa de Leyva.",
